From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:15:00 +1000
Subject: media: qcom: iris: Align the source size taken from a source change

iris_vdec_s_fmt() aligns the OUTPUT format to 32 for HEVC and to 16 for
other codecs, and the decoder's internal buffers are sized from it.
iris_hfi_gen2_read_input_subcr_params() then replaces it with the
unaligned bitstream resolution reported by the firmware. For an HEVC
stream whose height is not a multiple of 32, such as 1920x816, the BIN,
LINE and PARTIAL buffers are then allocated for 816 instead of 832
lines.

The new buffers are added to the ones from before the source change on
the first start, so decoding works, but when the OUTPUT queue is
restarted after a seek the firmware only gets the smaller set and fails
with HFI_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES. The failed restart then escalates
to a vb2 WARN and a list corruption oops on the next QBUF. Seen on a
Radxa Dragon Q6A with 1920x816 HEVC, Main and Main 10 alike.

Align the stored resolution as iris_vdec_s_fmt() does, and compute the
crop rectangle from the unaligned resolution so it still describes the
visible picture. This also makes the crop offsets sent to the firmware
the same before and after the source change; they were 16 lines at the
bottom before it and none after it.

The gen1 response handler stores the unaligned size too and gen1 sizes
its buffers from it, so it is likely affected as well; it is not
changed here as it is untested.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_response.c
@@ -534,6 +534,7 @@
 	u32 full_range, width, height;
 	struct vb2_queue *dst_q;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl;
+	u32 codec_align;
 
 	subsc_params = inst_hfi_gen2->src_subcr_params;
 	width = (subsc_params.bitstream_resolution &
@@ -541,8 +542,10 @@
 	height = subsc_params.bitstream_resolution &
 		HFI_BITMASK_BITSTREAM_HEIGHT;
 
-	pixmp_ip->width = width;
-	pixmp_ip->height = height;
+	/* aligned as in iris_vdec_s_fmt(), the internal buffers are sized from it */
+	codec_align = inst->codec == V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC ? 32 : 16;
+	pixmp_ip->width = ALIGN(width, codec_align);
+	pixmp_ip->height = ALIGN(height, codec_align);
 
 	if (subsc_params.bit_depth == BIT_DEPTH_8 &&
 	    pixmp_op->pixelformat != V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12 &&
@@ -609,9 +612,9 @@
 
 	inst->crop.top = subsc_params.crop_offsets[0] & 0xFFFF;
 	inst->crop.left = (subsc_params.crop_offsets[0] >> 16) & 0xFFFF;
-	inst->crop.height = pixmp_ip->height -
+	inst->crop.height = height -
 		(subsc_params.crop_offsets[1] & 0xFFFF) - inst->crop.top;
-	inst->crop.width = pixmp_ip->width -
+	inst->crop.width = width -
 		((subsc_params.crop_offsets[1] >> 16) & 0xFFFF) - inst->crop.left;
 
 	switch (inst->codec) {
